From 47ea4ef679826d2710d9bc727902d354c57a3f97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bandersong <134746909+bandersong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:17:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 27/44] MK2 step 1: DEVICE parameter and the MK2 control build
 (TRUTH D34, D35, D38)

make DEVICE=mk2 control builds the Analog Rytm MKII 1.73 stock MAIN OS back into
its ELE3 container and verifies it: null repack of the MKII stock .syx
byte-identical, MAIN OS round-trips, the four other sections (FPGA, bootstrap,
meta, 8) byte-identical to stock and to their analysed checksums, and the
embedded device firmware 0x402c8754..0x402cc91c unchanged.

tools/device.py: mk1 (default, every path as before) and mk2 (stock
Analog-Rytm_MKII_OS1.73.syx checked against stock/SHA256SUMS.mk2,
re/symbols_mk2.toml, registry/allocations_mk2.toml, build/mk2/, outputs
ARMK2_OS1.73_<tag>.syx, stubs assembled with DEVICE_MK2). build/verify/layout/
symbols take --device; layout also refuses any claim, patch or detour in a
never-write range. MK1-only targets refuse DEVICE=mk2.

MK1 outputs unchanged (guest, after this change): samplefocus 23a20937...,
samplefocus-cut 86e1dd1b..., control 3407638c..., default 0d51f7cb...,
random 3dafc0bd...; manifests, symbols.inc and ApplySymbols.java identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
