From bed4aa55776cb3cf4960a7eac8580a2e2871c80d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bandersong <134746909+bandersong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:21:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 28/44] MK2 step 2: Sample Focus CHOP on the MKII (make
 DEVICE=mk2 samplefocus; TRUTH D36, D37)

0000-shared lean (PROJ_KIT 352 on MK2) + 0001-chop for Analog Rytm MKII 1.73,
built and verified in the guest: PASS (null repack, round trip, the four other
sections byte-identical, embedded device firmware unchanged, 21 differing
regions all claimed, every detour re-emits or declares, every rejoin right).

MK2 differences, each under .ifdef DEVICE_MK2 so MK1 assembles as before:
- CHOP is page 12 (MK2 pages 0..11); page_info re-emits moveq #11.
- SAMP list {4, 5, 12} (count 0x400caf12 7202 -> 7203, list word 0x400caf18):
  stock's SAMPLE and SMPL WAVEFORM, then CHOP.
- No SAMPLE-key gate: every MK2 SAMPLE-key event reaches the base page cycle.
- samp_draw_gate, detour 0x400d1fa8 (tstl %a2@(140); bnes - reemit = false):
  the SAMP view draws page index != 0 with the waveform layout; page 12 is sent
  to the knob page draw (0x400d1fae), every other page goes where stock sends it.
- id 4's encoder template is 16 B on MK2: page_info_gate copies four longs
  (STA 0x401ed03c under HI, default 0x401ed07c under LO) to 0x419a49dc.
- MK2 symbols, PARAM_INFO_STRIDE 84, sta_value_text 0x400fbad8; expects re-read
  from the MK2 MAIN OS; ROM renames at MK1 + 0x31914 with MK2's string expects.
Layout A: .chst/.cave2 in cave (state at the end of .chst), .text/0000/.cave3
in cave2.

MK1 outputs unchanged (guest): samplefocus 23a20937..., samplefocus-cut
86e1dd1b..., control 3407638c..., default 0d51f7cb..., random 3dafc0bd...;
manifests identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
