+#         0x402ccc54  0008 .cutst  (run-time state: the filter state)
+#         0x402cccd4  0001 .chst   (the pad gates, chop_value, then CHOP's run-time state)
+#         0x402ccdf8  0001 .cave2  (the step lock and RND; MK1 has it in cave2)
+#   cave2 0x402cd8a0  0001 .text   (the page gates, samp_draw_gate, the knobs)
+#         0x402cdea0  0000 .text   (lean: shared_rnd, shared_sound_of, shared_mark_changed)
+#         0x402cdf2c  0001 .cave3  (constants: the SAMP page list, the CHOP descriptor,
+#                                   strings; MK1 has them in cave3)
+#   cave3 0x40289ab8  0008 .tab    (the cutoff table, helpers, page data; constants
+#                                   and code, no state)
+# cave and cave2 are 0xf78 apart, well inside bsr.w range, so .chst/.cave2 (cave) and
+# .text (cave2) call each other as on MK1; nothing branches to cave3 except by jsr.
