Subject: [PATCH 32/44] MK2 integrator: refuse a symbol map without its
 device's never-write range

corp mk2-panel-brick b1. tools/device.py protected(meta) returns [] when [meta]
has neither embedded_bootstrap_* nor never_write_* keys, and the layout, build
and verify checks that loop over it then passed without checking anything
(before devices, a missing key raised KeyError). Device.check_meta now refuses
such a map in layout.py, build.py and verify.py: MK1 must carry its embedded
bootstrap, MK2 its embedded device firmware and [meta.other_sections].

Guest: MK1 samplefocus 23a20937..., samplefocus-cut 86e1dd1b..., control
3407638c..., default 0d51f7cb..., random 3dafc0bd..., guard-check PASS; MK2
control f3f6aad0..., samplefocus 48fa678c..., samplefocus-cut 128b952e... PASS,
all byte-identical to before. Negative test on a guest throwaway copy: with the
keys stripped the old tools PASS (MK1 and MK2 control), the new ones refuse at
layout.py, build.py and verify.py (corp/mk2-integrator/neg/).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
