From 33ee7634d2e66b16aa1617f8120a2ae4350ff060 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bandersong <134746909+bandersong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 08:20:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 36/44] Keys step 1: DEVICE=keys profile and the Analog Keys
 control build (TRUTH K1, K5)

make DEVICE=keys control rebuilds the Analog Keys / Analog Four MK1 OS 1.56 stock
MAIN OS into its ELE2 container and verifies it (guest): null repack of the Keys
stock .syx byte-identical, MAIN OS round-trips, the rebuilt .syx carries MAIN OS
only like stock, the embedded bootstrap 0x40226ee8..0x40233fc0 unchanged (53,464 B,
recovery path) and the embedded UI-board firmware 0x401b8a92..0x401b9fd6 unchanged
(5,444 B), 0 differing regions. Output build/keys/AKEYS_OS1.56_control.syx
(sha256 6981fd94...).

tools/device.py: keys profile (stock/KEYS_Analog-Four_Analog-Keys_OS1.56.syx checked
against stock/SHA256SUMS.keys, re/symbols_keys.toml, registry/allocations_keys.toml,
build/keys/, AKEYS_ prefix, DEVICE_KEYS). check_meta requires BOTH Keys never-write
ranges (corp keys-platform P2/P3). Registry: the cave2 twin 0x4023485c..0x40235000
(probably-verified on MK1 cave2's static rule, re-derived for the Keys; first Keys
run promotes it) and the cave3 twin (candidate, unclaimed). Every Analog Rytm stub
now refuses to assemble under DEVICE_KEYS (keys-sk-platform C2); Rytm targets
refuse DEVICE=keys in the Makefile.

Rytm outputs unchanged (guest, after this change): MK1 samplefocus 76a2f4d0...,
samplefocus-cut 0ec86d0e..., control 3407638c..., default 0d51f7cb..., random
3dafc0bd...; MK2 control f3f6aad0..., samplefocus 016be9ea..., samplefocus-cut
0ce2fe92...; MK1 guard-check PASS; ApplySymbols.java unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
