Subject: [PATCH 37/44] Keys step 2: 0010-chord, chord memory for the Analog
 Keys (make DEVICE=keys chord; TRUTH K2-K4)

Hold 2..4 keybed keys, then FUNCTION + OCTAVE UP (code 164, no stock function: corp
keys-gesture + skeptic): the held notes (kind 1, state 1, the active track's,
per key its lowest, distinct, the lowest 4, each at most 63 semitones above the
root) become the chord in RAM and chord mode is on; popup "CHORD ON: 0 4 7"
(stock popup 0x40021774). The gesture with no key held turns chord mode off
("CHORD OFF"); with one key, nothing changes. While on, the KeyboardView note-on
0x400b9818 plays root + each interval, each through stock's own routine
(chord_stock = its displaced prologue + jmp 0x400b981e) with the same key id, so
stock's range check, duplicate guard, HOLD latch, voice/MIDI call and held entry
apply per tone and the key's release frees them all through stock 0x400b872e.
Pure stock when chord mode is off, inside a chord (chord_busy), and for every
note stock sends down its kind-2 path (stock's own test repeated;
keys-sk-notes plan problem 2).

Hooks: 0x400b9818 (expect 4e56ffa8707f, rejoin 0x400b981e) and 0x400b9e5c
(expect 0c83000000a4, re-emitted, rejoin 0x400b9e62); 678 B of code, strings
and 8 B of state in the cave2 twin at 0x4023485c (claim 0x2c0).

Guest: make DEVICE=keys chord PASS - build/keys/AKEYS_OS1.56_0010.syx sha256
b04c5680..., MAIN OS a6aab5cf...; 3 differing regions, all claimed; both
never-write ranges unchanged; displaced bytes re-emitted, rejoins correct.
Rytm outputs unchanged (guest, after this change): MK1 samplefocus 76a2f4d0...,
samplefocus-cut 0ec86d0e..., control 3407638c..., default 0d51f7cb..., random
3dafc0bd...; MK2 control f3f6aad0..., samplefocus 016be9ea..., samplefocus-cut
0ce2fe92...; Keys control 6981fd94... unchanged. make chord refuses on mk1/mk2.

