  alone (root included), so stock's duplicate guard no longer turns it into a held
  note under a key nobody holds. The check repeats stock's own predicate (kind 1
  track / kind 3 MIDI channel, note) and stands down when stock is about to release
  the latched notes itself (this+136 and HOLD down, 0x400b9874).
- purpose F1 / crash F2: chord_on records each call's note per key id
  (chord_root[128], RAM); the capture reads that note per held key, so re-capture
  with chord mode on gives the keys' intervals (C+G under 0 4 7: 0 7, was 0 11).
- crash F3 / purpose F2 (MIDI EXT part): a capture that counts nothing turns chord
  mode off only when no key is held; keys held that cannot be captured show
  "CHORD: NO CAPTURE HERE" and change nothing.
