From 52a611a4f4e2589ae9682204a47f3c68ec4efb03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bandersong <134746909+bandersong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:30:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 41/44] Keys 0010-chord K7: no chords around HOLD, orphan
 guard, OFF only when empty

TRUTH K7 (CEO 2026-10-08) after the keys-chord-v1 gate:
(a) chord_on plays no chord while the HOLD key is down or any held-table entry is
    HOLD-latched (state 2): the note goes to stock as one note. The old in-loop latch
    guard is gone; in its place an orphan guard on those paths does not send a note
    that stock's duplicate guard would merge into ANOTHER key's latched note (a hung
    note otherwise: latch a chord, then play one of its tones). It stands down when
    this+136 and HOLD are set (stock frees that latch first). Latched notes are
    never captured.
(b) The gesture turns chord mode OFF only when the table has no entry at all;
    keys held that cannot be captured -> "CHORD: NO CAPTURE HERE", only latched
    notes -> "CHORD: RELEASE HOLD FIRST"; 1 or 5+ keys -> "CHORD: HOLD 2-4 KEYS".
(c) Capture keeps reading the per-key-id root table chord_root.
(d) Tones above 127 skipped (now law; design.md no longer lists it as open).
(e) Keys cave2: the MK1-standard static proof re-derived (no reference at any byte
    offset, no loop walk, no store, below __bss_start, not cleared) and recorded in
    the registry pool note; claim 0x480 -> 0x500 (1192 B used).
(f) design.md test card: K6, K7 variant, K11 rewritten for HOLD, K11h/K11i (HOLD-on
    capture), K12 precondition, K13, K15 expectation, K18-K21 out of scope v1, the
    recovery route's Transfer step and the A4 MK1 wording.

Built and verified in the guest: make DEVICE=keys chord PASS
(AKEYS_OS1.56_0010.syx 02a4c784..., MAIN OS 17fa1afa...); Keys control 6981fd94
unchanged; every Rytm MK1/MK2 output byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
