From 634bd9072908fa7e6e2baa5d906b84698fa0e923 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bandersong <134746909+bandersong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:17:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 43/44] Keys 0010-chord: HOLD release-all read from the key
 scanner, stuck-note recovery, card order (K7 fix panel)

Corp keys-fix-integrator, on the K7 fix panel (keys-fix-panel-hold, keys-fix-panel-purpose).
Docs only; the image is unchanged.

- HOLD release-all: the branch at HOLD's release runs only on a clean tap (KeyEvent bit 4,
  set by the panel key scanner when the released key is the last panel key pressed,
  0x40062c46 / 0x40062d36 / 0x40062d3e), with FUNCTION up and this+136 still set (cleared
  when the press latched a held note, 0x400ba24e, or a note was played with HOLD down,
  0x400b9884). Replaces "bit 4 UNKNOWN" (panel-hold F1).
- Stuck-note recovery: release every key, tap HOLD twice (the first tap latches a note
  stock left held under a released key; the second releases it).
- HOLD fallback: use a key that is not a latched note (the orphan guard ignores E/G of a
  latched C chord, so HOLD's press finds no held entry). Re-latch documented, new card
  row K11j (panel-purpose F1).
- Summary: exact re-capture = release everything, gesture OFF, then capture (panel-purpose F3).
- Card: K11h/K11i run with chord on and end with a HOLD tap; K7 variant re-captures 0 4 7
  first; K12 trig keys out of scope v1 (no such mode in the Keys manual); K2 setup adds
  MULTI MAP off and keyboard transpose off (panel-purpose F2).
- README: Analog Keys section (build targets, Keys only, not yet staged in flash/).

Rebuilt in the guest: make DEVICE=keys chord PASS (AKEYS_OS1.56_0010.syx 02a4c784...,
MAIN OS 17fa1afa...), Keys control 6981fd94..., MK1 76a2f4d0/0ec86d0e/3407638c,
MK2 f3f6aad0/016be9ea/0ce2fe92 - every output byte-identical to before.

